.TH ORO-TAR 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:tar \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:tar'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
High\-level helpers for reading and writing tar archives.
.PP
This module is designed for very large archives and supports: \- Streaming decode via range reads on individual entries \- Streaming encode via chunked entry writes \- Optional `mmap`\-backed indexing on supported native platforms \- Random access to entries by path
.PP
Example: import * as tar from 'oro:tar'
.PP
const archive = await tar.open('./assets.tar') const entries = await archive.entries() const buf = await archive.read('images/logo.png')
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBTarArchive\fR
Represents an open tar archive on disk.
.TP
\fBopen(path, options)\fR
Opens an existing tar archive.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpath\fR (string \\| URL; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (TarOpenOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<TarArchive>\fR
.TP
\fBcreate(path, options)\fR
Creates a new tar archive for writing. If the archive already exists it will be truncated.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpath\fR (string \\| URL; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (TarOpenOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<TarArchive>\fR
.TP
\fBfromBuffer(buffer)\fR
Opens a tar archive from an in\-memory buffer (read\-only).
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIbuffer\fR (Buffer \\| Uint8Array \\| ArrayBuffer; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<TarArchive>\fR
.TP
\fBcreateInMemory(options)\fR
Creates a new in\-memory tar archive for writing.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (TarOpenOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<TarArchive>\fR
.TP
\fBclose()\fR
Closes the underlying archive descriptor. Further operations on this instance will throw.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBentries()\fR
Lists all entries in the archive.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<TarEntryStat[]>\fR
.TP
\fBextractAll(destDir, options)\fR
Extracts all file and directory entries in the archive into a destination directory using streaming. Attempts to preserve mode/mtime metadata.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIdestDir\fR (string \\| URL; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR ({ signal?: AbortSignal, timeout?: number, filter?: (entry: TarEntryStat) => boolean, preserveLinks?: boolean, preserveOwner?: boolean, preserveSpecialModes?: boolean }; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBstat(entryPath)\fR
Returns metadata for a single entry path.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIentryPath\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<TarEntryStat>\fR
.TP
\fBread(path, options)\fR
Reads a slice of an entry as a Buffer.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpath\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (TarReadOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<Buffer>\fR
.TP
\fBreadStream(path, options)\fR
Creates an async iterator that yields Buffer chunks for a given entry. This provides a streaming decode interface without requiring Node.js streams.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpath\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (TarReadStreamOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIAsyncIterableIterator<Buffer>\fR
.TP
\fBappend(header, body, options)\fR
Appends a single entry to the archive. The entry body can be a Buffer, ArrayBuffer, Uint8Array, or an async iterable of Buffers.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIheader\fR (TarEntryHeader; required)
.br
\fIbody\fR (Buffer \\| Uint8Array \\| ArrayBuffer \\| AsyncIterable<Buffer \\| Uint8Array>; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (TarWriteOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBfinalize()\fR
Finalizes the archive, writing terminating blocks and flushing the sink. After calling this, the archive is still considered open but no further writes should be performed.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBtoBuffer(options)\fR
Finalizes the archive if necessary and returns the underlying tar archive bytes as a Buffer. For in\-memory writable archives this contains the composed archive; for read\-only archives created via fromBuffer it returns the original buffer.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR ({ signal?: AbortSignal, timeout?: number }; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<Buffer>\fR
.TP
\fBextract(path, destPath, options)\fR
Extracts a single entry to a destination path on disk. This helper uses streaming reads for large entries.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpath\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIdestPath\fR (string \\| URL; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR ({ signal?: AbortSignal, timeout?: number, preserveOwner?: boolean, preserveSpecialModes?: boolean }; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBopen(path, options)\fR
Opens an existing tar archive.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpath\fR (string \\| URL; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (TarOpenOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<TarArchive>\fR
.TP
\fBcreate(path, options)\fR
Creates a new tar archive for writing. If the archive already exists it will be truncated.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpath\fR (string \\| URL; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (TarOpenOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<TarArchive>\fR
.TP
\fBfromBuffer(buffer)\fR
Opens a tar archive from an in\-memory buffer (read\-only).
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIbuffer\fR (Buffer \\| Uint8Array \\| ArrayBuffer; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<TarArchive>\fR
.TP
\fBcreateInMemory(options)\fR
Creates a new in\-memory tar archive for writing.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (TarOpenOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<TarArchive>\fR
